"Let $G$ be an infinite graph with vertex set $E$. For distinct vertices $x,y\\in E$, write $G|E\\setminus\\{x\\}$ for the subgraph induced by deleting $x$, and write $\\sim$ for graph isomorphism. **Ulam reconstruction conjecture.** If\n\n$$\n\\forall (x,y)\\in E^2,\\quad x\\neq y;\\quad G|E\\setminus\\{x\\}\\sim G|E\\setminus\\{y\\},\n$$\n\nthen $G$ is Ulam-reconstructible. The source presents this as a conjectural sufficient condition for infinite-graph reconstruction, with no supplied resolution."